# 2026-07-26 (quality-mgr, AICH-S7-QA-FIX-2): arch-ctm's self-reported forward-merge
# fix e1b754b5 on feature/pAI-s28-bounded-peer-recovery does NOT touch runtime_health.rs
# at all (git show --stat e1b754b5: peer_delivery_observability.rs, peer_drain_coordinator.rs,
# runtime_health/peer_delivery_router.rs, tests/runtime_root/peer_observability.rs only).
# Independently re-confirmed via git show origin/feature/pAI-s28-bounded-peer-recovery
# (and identically on s29, inherited via 7e73866a): the Local ingress arm at
# runtime_health.rs:899-902 only rejects on origin_message_id/origin_timestamp presence;
# authenticated_source_host is neither checked nor stripped on Local ingress. The
# s28-regressed-2d7ca600/s29-regressed-ab442ac3 occurrences below remain live and
# UNFIXED by this commit chain. Task #1145 (fix AI23-BLOCK-002 regression on s28) is
# still open; arch-ctm's "just test PASS" self-report did not address this finding.
# s30 (b4b304d0, current head unchanged from prior b7ad9f6c verification) remains fixed.

# 2026-07-26 (quality-mgr, arch-ctm audit evidence re-verification): arch-ctm reported
# (message 01KYG2HZWP9YXBXEJDR06M6RAF) that AI23-BLOCK-002 is not an open occurrence
# on feature/pAI-s27-peer-delivery-observability current HEAD fb1994b9. Independently
# confirmed by direct git show: runtime_health.rs:876-892 rejects Local writes carrying
# authenticated_source_host/origin_message_id/origin_timestamp and requires all 3 fields
# for Peer ingress; send/mod.rs:323-325 is_peer_receipt() delegates to
# has_authenticated_peer_provenance() (send/mod.rs:597-601), a 3-field AND. Matches
# arch-ctm's claim exactly. New s27-fixed-fb1994b9 occurrence added below superseding
# the stale f378a830 snapshot. This does NOT close the top-level finding -- s28/s29
# regressed occurrences above remain open and are the actual live blockers; arch-ctm's
# message states he is addressing those plus a separate Windows regression.

# 2026-07-26 (quality-mgr, AICH-S10-QA-FWDMERGE-2, PR #623 fwd-merge sweep):
# REGRESSION FOUND. Merge 2d7ca600 (feature/pAI-s27-peer-delivery-observability
# -> feature/pAI-s28-bounded-peer-recovery) resolved runtime_health.rs entirely
# in favor of s28's own pre-fix content (git diff 2d7ca600^1 2d7ca600 --
# runtime_health.rs is empty) -- s27's fix (f378a830) was silently dropped
# during the merge, not intentionally reverted. s29 (ab442ac3) inherited the
# regression unfixed from s28; s30 (3c46f917) is unaffected because it already
# carried its own independent fix before merging s29 in. Do NOT close s25/s30
# occurrences by assuming s26-s29 propagation from ancestry alone -- that
# assumption is exactly what broke here. highestOpenBranch/promoteToBranch
# moved to s28 (earliest affected, root cause of the regression); fix must
# land there first, then forward-merge to s29.

# 2026-07-26 (quality-mgr, AICH-S9-QA-FWDMERGE-1, PR #623): re-verified against
# feature/pAI-s30-semver-http-compatibility CURRENT HEAD b7ad9f6c (the recorded
# s30-primary/s30-secondary occurrences below are STALE -- headSha 9fd44444
# predates arch-ctm's forward-merge sweep AI25->AI26->AI27->AI28->AI29->AI30).
# Independently confirmed (quality-mgr direct grep + ruthless-boundary-qa,
# 2 sources agree): the s30-secondary-is-peer-receipt occurrence's own snippet
# and note cite function names (is_authenticated_peer_receipt,
# is_same_host_peer_receipt) and a regression test
# (local_write_rejects_forged_peer_provenance at runtime_health.rs:1136-1168)
# that do NOT exist anywhere in the current worktree, and quote code
# (`authenticated_source_host.is_some() || origin_message_id.is_some()`) that
# does not match the real function at send/mod.rs:597-601. This looks like
# stale/fabricated content carried over from an already-fixed finding rather
# than a live re-derivation against s30. On CURRENT s30 HEAD (b7ad9f6c):
# ApiRouter::route (runtime_health.rs:915,923,932) strips authenticated_source_host
# on Local ingress and requires all 3 fields on Peer ingress; is_peer_receipt()
# (send/mod.rs:323-325) delegates to has_authenticated_peer_provenance()
# (send/mod.rs:597-601), a 3-field AND, not a bare is_some(). authenticated_source_host
# is set to Some(...) only after TLS peer authentication (https_transport.rs:549,627)
# and is explicitly nulled on local/untrusted ingress. Both the primary and
# secondary occurrences are FIXED on s30's current head. Top-level status
# remains "open" ONLY because s26-s29 have not been independently re-verified
# against their own CURRENT heads this round (this task's scope was the s30
# forward-merge, not a full re-triage) -- given s23-s30 form a linear branch
# lineage (each sprint branched from the prior), it is likely s26-s29 already
# carry this fix too, but that must be confirmed by a dedicated re-triage pass,
# not assumed. Recommend team-lead schedule that follow-up sweep; also recommend
# auditing other .ttl records for similarly stale/fabricated occurrence content.

# Closure note: s22-primary and s23 occurrences confirmed fixed at root/introduction site.
# Round-2 fix verified on feature/pAI-s23-crosshost-shared-write-path @ b0781316.
# Validated by 3 independent reviewers (quality-mgr, rust-qa-agent, team-lead).
# Root cause (authenticated_source_host bare is_some() check) now replaced with ALL THREE field AND logic.
#
# 2026-07-26 (quality-mgr): AI.23 merged into integrate/phase-AI via PR #629
# (merge commit 8750587b3e24c6e5a18e14315c363b6ea0f2d8e0). Independently
# re-verified against integrate/phase-AI HEAD: ApiRouter::route
# (runtime_health.rs:919-931) now rejects Local writes carrying
# authenticated_source_host (not just origin_message_id/origin_timestamp) and
# requires all 3 provenance fields on Peer ingress; is_peer_receipt()
# (send/mod.rs:311-313) delegates to has_authenticated_peer_provenance()
# (send/mod.rs:570-574), which ANDs all 3 fields, replacing the vulnerable
# bare is_some() check entirely. Regression test
# local_write_rejects_forged_peer_provenance present (runtime_health.rs:1137).
# This is NOT an unresolved AI.23 blocker on the current integration branch --
# the s25/s30 occurrences below are stale pre-merge-forward snapshots on
# branches that have not yet merged this fix forward themselves; status
# remains "open" at the top level only to track that cascade, not because the
# fix is missing on integrate/phase-AI.

